<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantius-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-28">28 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Constantius II makes his only visit to Rome</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in triumph for the first time. The historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ammianus-marcellinus">Ammianus Marcellinus</a> described his astonishment at the Forum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a> and other monuments.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantius-ii">Constantius II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-strasbourg">Battle of Strasbourg</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Strasbourg, or Argentoratum, was fought in August 357 near Strasbourg between a Roman army under the Caesar Julian and a coalition of Alemannic kings led by Chnodomar and his nephew Serapio.</p></div></li></ol></section>
